            <ArticleTitle>An Old-Fashioned Notion: Stand Behind Your Wares.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Experience from the field suggests that measuring the outcomes that underpin risk-based contracts is not always as simple as it sounds. There are many practical challenges to value-based contracts: administrative overhead, the intricacies of data collection and validation, and understanding how or why the data are relevant to the agreement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
